WEBVTT

00:02.790 --> 00:04.480
Mother, I'm so sorry...

00:05.440 --> 00:09.820
Your precious brooch was stolen by Rosso and Bianco.

00:10.940 --> 00:13.200
But just you wait! I'll definitely get it back!

00:13.990 --> 00:16.820
For that reason, we've returned to Europe.

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.120 --> 01:58.160
Rome, Italy

01:59.700 --> 02:03.450
﻿Because I let my guard down. Mother's brooch was stolen...

02:07.790 --> 02:10.920
﻿It looks like it'll still be awhile before we head to Vienna.

02:10.920 --> 02:15.710
﻿We're going to perform in Rome for a while and earn some money to get us to Vienna.

02:16.380 --> 02:19.760
There's no helping it/ If we don't have money, we can't really travel around.

02:20.760 --> 02:22.760
﻿Cheer up, Nadja.

02:22.760 --> 02:26.180
﻿We'll definitely get your brooch back!

02:27.100 --> 02:28.100
﻿Thank you...

02:28.600 --> 02:31.810
﻿Even if I don't have my brooch, I still have the diary and dress.

02:31.810 --> 02:33.810
﻿And I have plenty of clues leading to Mom!

02:34.440 --> 02:38.400
﻿But who was the one who hired those two to steal the brooch...?

02:38.740 --> 02:41.990
I'm sure Rosso and that person are also in Vienna.

02:41.990 --> 02:43.820
﻿I have to hurry and get there!

02:54.500 --> 02:56.300
﻿She fell.

02:56.590 --> 02:58.630
﻿Well, they are just traveling entertainers after all.

02:58.630 --> 03:00.340
﻿Watching them alone is a waste of time.

03:09.790 --> 03:14.790
Farewell, Dandelion Troupe

03:15.480 --> 03:17.320
﻿This is all we earned today...

03:17.690 --> 03:20.900
﻿This will definitely affect tomorrow's turnout too...

03:20.900 --> 03:23.030
I'﻿m sorry ... because of me...

03:23.030 --> 03:25.700
Do you think you can make up for this by simply apologizing?

03:26.120 --> 03:29.080
When you were dancing, you were thinking of other things, weren't you?

03:29.080 --> 03:30.120
That is very unprofessional.

03:30.580 --> 03:32.580
﻿What's gotten into you, Thomas?

03:32.580 --> 03:35.920
﻿When it comes to the performances, Thomas is always the loudest one.

03:36.340 --> 03:38.920
I'm just stating the obvious!

03:39.170 --> 03:44.010
﻿Her mothers brooch was stolen. Of course she'd be distracted by it.

03:44.010 --> 03:48.060
﻿No matter what reason she has, it shouldn't be an excuse for messing up!

03:48.970 --> 03:49.680
﻿Now, now.

03:49.980 --> 03:53.810
﻿To make this short, you want to get to Vienna as soon as possible, right Nadja?

03:54.230 --> 03:56.520
﻿Then why don't we just leave for there right away?

03:57.980 --> 04:00.030
﻿If you're worried about supplies, then we have enough for the both of us!

04:00.990 --> 04:03.450
﻿Let's hop on the mechanical car and go to Vienna!

04:03.700 --> 04:07.320
﻿Wait, wait! In that time, what are we all supposed to do?

04:07.330 --> 04:09.410
﻿You can just camp out around here or something!

04:09.620 --> 04:11.160
﻿Like heck we can!

04:11.160 --> 04:14.420
﻿We should all earn the money and go together!

04:14.790 --> 04:16.290
﻿If it's money you need, there's some right here...

04:16.380 --> 04:16.920
﻿See?

04:17.170 --> 04:18.250
﻿What?!

04:19.550 --> 04:21.340
﻿What is all of this?

04:21.340 --> 04:22.970
﻿I found it underneath the sofa!

04:23.550 --> 04:26.680
﻿Thank goodness! Now we can go to Vienna right away!

04:27.100 --> 04:28.470
﻿It's cursed!

04:28.720 --> 04:32.850
﻿This crystal ball is telling me to tell you to return that money to where you found it!

04:32.980 --> 04:34.560
﻿That was your secret stash, wasn't it Granny?!

04:35.600 --> 04:36.600
﻿U-Umm...

04:36.610 --> 04:41.940
﻿So, you were saving quite a bit of money and keeping it from the rest of us, weren't you?

04:41.940 --> 04:44.700
﻿Granny, is this all of your stash?

04:44.700 --> 04:48.410
﻿But... that's the money I earned from making my hats...

04:47.430 --> 04:48.930
Everyone, calm down!

04:48.410 --> 04:51.870
﻿I was holding it for a case of an emergency when the troupe really needed it.

04:49.760 --> 04:50.810
Calm down!

04:51.470 --> 04:52.810
Calm down!

04:52.830 --> 04:54.960
﻿Now's that time of emergency, isn't it?!

04:55.330 --> 04:56.500
﻿Master!

04:56.750 --> 04:59.670
﻿I trust all of you aren't hiding money like this, right?

05:00.750 --> 05:03.590
﻿Ah! Sylvie... you bought new lipstick not too long ago, didn't you?

05:03.590 --> 05:05.630
﻿You couldn't have bought that without money...

05:05.630 --> 05:09.390
﻿W-What about you? Didn't you buy some new shoes?

05:09.810 --> 05:13.430
﻿That was on a special sale, so...!

05:14.430 --> 05:16.600
﻿Nadja, use this!

05:18.310 --> 05:20.610
﻿It's all of the allowance I've saved up till now.

05:20.610 --> 05:22.360
﻿You can go to Vienna with this, right?

05:24.280 --> 05:25.030
﻿Rita...

05:27.570 --> 05:30.450
﻿Sorry. This is all I have.

05:30.870 --> 05:33.540
﻿Not at all... I'm happy with just that. Thank you.

05:34.540 --> 05:38.210
﻿J-Just look at these praiseworthy kids.

05:38.210 --> 05:40.250
﻿You dirty adults.

05:40.590 --> 05:44.460
﻿Speak for yourself! It's not like you pulled out your allowance to give to her!

05:44.510 --> 05:47.340
﻿Not that I mean to brag or anything, but I am penniless!

05:47.590 --> 05:49.640
﻿That's nothing to be proud about

05:49.640 --> 05:51.850
﻿I may not have money, but I have a man's spirit!

05:51.850 --> 05:54.720
﻿A man's spirit alone won't put food on your plate.

05:55.680 --> 05:56.850
﻿Hmph, I can still eat it!

05:56.850 --> 05:59.060
﻿We're not getting anywhere like this.

06:00.900 --> 06:02.270
﻿H-Hold on! Everyone!

06:06.740 --> 06:08.110
﻿They won't come...

06:08.860 --> 06:12.410
﻿If it were like normal, this is the time when everyone would gather to have tea.

06:12.830 --> 06:14.240
Isn't it good?

06:15.620 --> 06:17.620
﻿Adults are so stubborn.

06:18.040 --> 06:20.880
﻿We somehow have to make everyone make up with each other!

06:20.880 --> 06:23.090
﻿Kennosuke, will you help me

06:23.840 --> 06:26.050
I knew you'd say something like that, Nadja!

06:28.630 --> 06:32.090
﻿No one cares about the elderly these days!

06:32.100 --> 06:35.640
﻿Especially that George! Ever since he was a kid, he was always like this!

06:35.640 --> 06:38.310
﻿My goodness, he is a selfish man!

06:38.310 --> 06:40.440
﻿What was Master like as a kid?

06:40.440 --> 06:42.190
﻿A skinny little twig is what he was.

06:42.190 --> 06:44.480
﻿Master was skinny?!

06:45.900 --> 06:47.610
﻿Just wait a little longer, Nadja.

06:47.610 --> 06:52.070
﻿I'll make some new hats, and earn us money to go to Vienna right away.

06:52.570 --> 06:56.870
﻿No. Why do I have to apologize?

06:56.870 --> 06:58.250
﻿You're our leader, aren't you?!

06:58.250 --> 06:59.500
﻿No means no.

06:59.500 --> 07:01.580
﻿Oh, this brings backs memories.

07:01.580 --> 07:02.290
﻿Take a look at this.

07:03.880 --> 07:05.540
﻿Is this Sylvie?

07:05.550 --> 07:07.460
﻿No way. She looks like her, but take a look here!

07:07.460 --> 07:09.550
﻿She has no mole underneath her eye.

07:09.930 --> 07:11.050
﻿That's Granny.

07:11.050 --> 07:12.470
﻿Granny?!

07:12.470 --> 07:13.430
﻿No way...

07:13.430 --> 07:14.890
﻿It can't be...

07:14.930 --> 07:17.560
﻿How did she shrink so much?!

07:20.520 --> 07:21.890
﻿All right, here it is!

07:21.900 --> 07:23.850
﻿Take a look here. Just you wait, Nadja!

07:23.860 --> 07:27.900
﻿I'll find this treasure and take you to Vienna or wherever you want!

07:28.440 --> 07:32.110
﻿If we waited for something like that, we'd be stuck here for the rest of our lives...

07:37.160 --> 07:41.040
﻿I'm truly sorry... so please make up with everyone!

07:42.830 --> 07:45.000
﻿Nadja, shouldn't you be practicing your dance?

07:47.630 --> 07:50.760
﻿You used to practice dancing every day.

07:50.760 --> 07:53.800
﻿but ever since your brooch was stolen, you've stopped doing so.

07:54.590 --> 07:56.550
﻿That's why you messed up.

07:56.550 --> 07:59.930
﻿Don't sound so high and mighty as if you were so much better than her!

08:00.730 --> 08:05.060
﻿You've messed up plenty of times to date, and even been boo-ed at!

08:05.060 --> 08:06.650
﻿You have too!

08:07.190 --> 08:08.230
﻿Stop this you two!

08:10.610 --> 08:13.200
﻿Abel! Thomas!

08:13.200 --> 08:15.160
﻿Both of them sure are skilled aren't they?

08:15.160 --> 08:17.950
﻿They managed to practice like that and fight at the same time.

08:18.620 --> 08:21.160
﻿Please make up with everyone!

08:21.710 --> 08:24.710
If there's anything I can do, 'll do anything!

08:27.500 --> 08:30.090
﻿Then will you join me in my shopping?

08:30.090 --> 08:31.090
﻿Shopping?

08:31.760 --> 08:34.800
﻿Everyone's so mad because they're all hungry.

08:34.800 --> 08:38.300
﻿I'll make one heck of a feast for everyone.

08:38.300 --> 08:42.810
﻿If everyone eats something good together, we'll all be made up in an instant.

08:42.810 --> 08:43.930
﻿Yeah!

08:47.360 --> 08:49.800
﻿What is this feast?

08:49.800 --> 08:51.030
No, now, eat up.

08:51.030 --> 08:54.530
﻿What are you doing, making something like this when we have no money to spare?!

08:54.530 --> 08:56.910
﻿At times like this, we should be economizing!

08:56.910 --> 09:00.870
﻿Yeah! You can't make trivial expenses like this, Sylvie!

09:00.870 --> 09:04.540
﻿I'll never make food for any of you ever again!

09:04.910 --> 09:06.250
﻿No way...

09:06.670 --> 09:10.460
﻿In the first place, why are we so broke?!

09:10.460 --> 09:12.960
﻿Because of all of your treasure hunts, George!

09:13.670 --> 09:18.090
﻿Yeah! It's because you waste so much money on your utterly useless treasure hunts!

09:19.140 --> 09:22.100
﻿Searching for treasure is a man's romance!

09:22.100 --> 09:22.890
﻿Right?

09:22.890 --> 09:26.770
I ﻿might be a man, but I would prefer if you didn't group me together with you.

09:27.650 --> 09:29.350
﻿E-Everyone! Please stop fighting!

09:29.360 --> 09:31.690
﻿Romance alone won't let us eat!

09:31.860 --> 09:32.820
﻿What?!

09:33.030 --> 09:35.150
﻿Neither of you are real men!

09:35.150 --> 09:37.030
﻿STOP FIGHTING!

09:37.320 --> 09:41.240
﻿Nadja! This all started because you messed up your performance!

09:42.120 --> 09:44.330
﻿Thomas, would you lay off?

09:48.370 --> 09:51.790
﻿My meal...! After I went through the trouble to cook it all!

09:51.800 --> 09:54.340
﻿Before worrying about the food, would you please worry some about me?

09:54.340 --> 09:57.050
﻿What are you all doing, putting this food to waste?!

09:57.050 --> 09:58.720
﻿We don't have enough money for all this!

09:58.720 --> 10:00.390
﻿Shut up, all of you!

10:01.810 --> 10:04.350
﻿I can't continue with all of you like this any longer!

10:04.350 --> 10:07.850
﻿As of today, the Dandelion Troupe has been disbanded!

10:09.060 --> 10:10.100
﻿Yeah!

10:10.110 --> 10:11.110
﻿Sounds good to me!

10:11.110 --> 10:12.730
﻿That'd be best!

10:14.780 --> 10:16.030
﻿No way...

10:39.800 --> 10:40.840
﻿Dear Miss Appleton,

10:41.680 --> 10:46.310
﻿Because of my slip-up, everyone in the troupe has split apart.

10:46.770 --> 10:49.770
﻿What can I do to make everyone get back together...?

10:52.650 --> 10:54.400
﻿Rita, why don't you go to bed?

10:54.400 --> 10:55.650
﻿Yeah.

10:57.440 --> 10:59.700
﻿You printed that many fliers?

10:59.860 --> 11:03.660
﻿If we hand out a lot, lots of customers will come to see us, right?

11:04.740 --> 11:06.370
﻿I wonder if we'll be able to do the performance...

11:06.580 --> 11:10.330
﻿It'll be fine! By tomorrow, everyone will be getting along again.

11:11.080 --> 11:12.580
﻿Yeah. You're right.

11:13.380 --> 11:15.040
﻿Then... good night, Nadja.

11:15.300 --> 11:17.250
﻿Good night, Rita.

11:17.260 --> 11:18.010
All right...!

11:18.880 --> 11:21.880
﻿It's just as Rita said. By tomorrow...

11:21.890 --> 11:24.260
﻿That's why I was so against it back then.

11:24.260 --> 11:26.910
﻿Shh. Quiet down some.

11:26.910 --> 11:28.930
The kids will hear you.

11:31.900 --> 11:33.940
﻿I was also against it.

11:37.860 --> 11:41.780
﻿Really... we never should've let Nadja join the troupe.

11:43.620 --> 11:45.450
﻿Yeah...

11:45.450 --> 11:49.450
﻿If we never let Nadja in the Troupe in the first place, this wouldn't have happened.

12:00.800 --> 12:02.930
﻿Because of those two scoundrels... Rosso and Bianco.

12:03.760 --> 12:08.510
﻿They're using the troupe as their sign to point to Nadja.

12:09.100 --> 12:12.980
﻿If we hadn't let her enter the troupe, she might've still had her brooch right now.

12:13.560 --> 12:16.360
﻿Though we can't really do much about what has already come to pass...

12:16.360 --> 12:17.690
﻿All we can do is regret.

12:18.270 --> 12:20.150
﻿I wonder how long it's been...

12:21.360 --> 12:26.870
I ﻿was just wondering how many months have passed since Nadja joined our troupe.

12:26.870 --> 12:29.790
﻿It still hasn't even been a year, right?

12:29.790 --> 12:32.200
﻿But it feels like we've been with her for years.

12:32.750 --> 12:37.920
﻿I can't even think of the Dandelion Troupe without her dancing.

12:37.920 --> 12:41.880
﻿It's so hard to believe that before this incident, she didn't even mess up once.

12:42.340 --> 12:45.380
﻿Nadja's completely different from the rest of you.

12:45.390 --> 12:46.680
﻿That includes you.

12:57.150 --> 12:59.190
﻿Everyone, come get a plate.

12:59.190 --> 13:01.070
﻿Sylvie, I'll have a large portion!

13:01.070 --> 13:03.490
﻿You're already eating too much straight from this morning, Master.

13:03.470 --> 13:07.140
Well I can't hold the performance on an empty stomach!

13:03.490 --> 13:07.160
﻿Huh? When did everyone start getting along with each other again?

13:08.660 --> 13:11.830
﻿We can't just stay4ighting forever.

13:11.830 --> 13:15.660
﻿We have to earn us as much money as fast as we can so we can get to Vienna.

13:15.670 --> 13:17.120
﻿That's pretty much it.

13:17.380 --> 13:19.920
﻿Kennosuke, could you wake Nadja?

13:19.920 --> 13:21.040
﻿Okay!

13:21.250 --> 13:24.210
﻿Nadja! Nadja... wake up!

13:24.720 --> 13:26.430
﻿Huh? She's not here.

13:27.510 --> 13:28.760
﻿What's this?

13:29.220 --> 13:30.510
Big trouble!!

13:33.100 --> 13:39.480
﻿l've been happy with you. Thank you for everything. Good bye. -Nadja."

13:40.320 --> 13:41.520
﻿That girl...!

13:49.700 --> 13:54.490
I'﻿ve gone to so many countries and experienced traveling all over.

13:54.500 --> 13:56.160
I can make it on my own.

14:00.210 --> 14:01.790
﻿Everything was so much fun...

14:15.060 --> 14:18.020
﻿I wonder how much farther I have to go to reach Vienna...

14:22.610 --> 14:24.110
﻿I'm hungry.

14:26.190 --> 14:28.780
﻿I wonder if everyone's eating breakfast right about now?

14:44.880 --> 14:47.300
﻿Boss, are you sure you're not going the wrong way?

14:47.300 --> 14:50.930
﻿No... if she was heading straight to Vienna, this is the only road.

14:57.640 --> 14:59.480
﻿Goodbye, everyone..

15:07.440 --> 15:09.440
﻿Creme? Chocolat?

15:19.540 --> 15:21.920
﻿Creme, Chocolat! Let go!

15:29.260 --> 15:30.300
﻿Nadja!

15:31.300 --> 15:32.880
﻿What's the meaning of this?

15:33.850 --> 15:36.260
﻿It's just as I wrote. It's a letter of goodbye.

15:36.260 --> 15:37.930
﻿You moron!

15:39.310 --> 15:42.190
﻿No one can leave without the Master's permission!

15:42.770 --> 15:45.310
﻿Hurry and get back and prepare for the performance!

15:45.860 --> 15:47.150
﻿The performance?

15:47.150 --> 15:49.070
﻿Then the troupe isn't disbanded?

15:49.070 --> 15:50.940
﻿Disbanded? What are you talking about?

15:52.030 --> 15:55.780
﻿It's not uncommon to hear him say things like disbanding the troupe.

15:55.780 --> 15:58.910
﻿Even if it's the smallest fight, he'll jump right to saying things like that.

15:58.910 --> 16:03.920
﻿Once he says it, he won't listen to anyone, but he's quick to forget about it.

16:03.920 --> 16:05.330
﻿Nadja, let's go back together!

16:06.230 --> 16:07.360
No...

16:07.800 --> 16:09.130
﻿Nadja...

16:09.130 --> 16:11.130
﻿You're pretty stubborn yourself.

16:11.130 --> 16:13.590
﻿If I'm with you all, I'm just a nuisance, right?

16:14.800 --> 16:17.260
I ﻿overheard all of you talking yesterday night.

16:17.720 --> 16:20.180
﻿That it would've been better if you never let me in the troupe in the first place.

16:21.770 --> 16:24.020
Oh, silly. There's more to it.

16:24.150 --> 16:25.230
﻿Goodbye!

16:26.190 --> 16:29.110
﻿Nadia , you have to take responsibility.

16:31.650 --> 16:34.860
﻿We'll have you take responsibility for messing up in the performance.

16:34.860 --> 16:36.570
﻿It's not something you can make up for by apologizing.

16:37.120 --> 16:41.540
﻿Dance wonderfully like you always do and bring our customers back.

16:43.540 --> 16:47.130
﻿That's how I always make reparations when I mess up.

16:48.250 --> 16:52.170
﻿If you show a good performance, customers will return naturally.

16:52.510 --> 16:53.800
﻿But...

16:53.800 --> 16:56.380
﻿I calculated how much money we'll need to get to Vienna.

16:56.390 --> 16:59.930
﻿If we do our best and perform well for another six days, I think we'll have enough.

16:59.930 --> 17:02.560
﻿And if we do two performances a day, that'll make it three days.

17:02.930 --> 17:05.730
﻿Once we gather up all the money, it's straight to Vienna with us!

17:05.730 --> 17:09.020
﻿I think that if we all work hard together for the next three days and go in the car,

17:09.020 --> 17:11.070
﻿it will be faster than walking all by yourself.

17:12.150 --> 17:14.280
﻿I'm sure I'll be troublesome again...

17:14.700 --> 17:17.240
﻿There's no one in this world who's never not troublesome.

17:17.870 --> 17:20.490
﻿It'd actually be better if you'd caused some more trouble.

17:20.490 --> 17:23.870
﻿If I were you, I'd really want to stir amuck!

17:23.870 --> 17:25.830
﻿Oh, you little...

17:27.830 --> 17:31.040
﻿But anyway, that fight was sure the first one in awhile.

17:31.050 --> 17:33.050
﻿I feel so refreshed after saying what I wanted to.

17:33.710 --> 17:36.170
﻿Every now and then, we have to really express ourselves.

17:36.970 --> 17:40.220
And now everyone has, Nadja.

17:40.220 --> 17:41.140
﻿Why don't you do too?

17:44.640 --> 17:46.810
﻿Do you really want to go all alone?

17:47.730 --> 17:48.650
﻿I...

17:53.190 --> 17:54.230
﻿I...

17:55.990 --> 17:57.700
﻿I want to be with everyone..

17:58.360 --> 17:59.700
﻿Me too.

17:59.700 --> 18:00.570
﻿Don't forget me.

18:01.080 --> 18:02.330
﻿Or me!

18:02.330 --> 18:04.080
﻿That's obvious!

18:04.580 --> 18:06.000
﻿Since were all family.

18:06.000 --> 18:07.210
﻿Yep!

18:07.670 --> 18:10.130
﻿Everyone feels the same way.

18:11.540 --> 18:12.540
﻿Thank you...

18:13.920 --> 18:15.510
﻿Everyone, thank you!

18:44.240 --> 18:46.240
﻿I don i know what will happen from this point on.

18:47.790 --> 18:52.130
﻿I want to hurry and get my brooch back and I want to get to Vienna as soon as I can.

18:52.130 --> 18:54.750
﻿I might be a little impatient, but...

18:56.380 --> 18:58.840
﻿But I'm sure everything will be all right.

18:58.840 --> 19:01.260
﻿I can think that way for sure.

19:01.260 --> 19:04.010
﻿Because everyone's here for me.

19:05.310 --> 19:09.770
﻿I'm... so glad I joined the Dandelion Troupe!

19:28.890 --> 19:31.900
Vienna, Herman's Mansion

19:30.520 --> 19:35.110
Lord Herman, this is Nadja's brooch and ring.

19:40.220 --> 19:41.630
﻿There's no doubt about it.

19:41.630 --> 19:44.430
﻿This is indeed the crest of arms of the Ducal House of Preminger.

19:44.850 --> 19:46.760
Boss, we did it!

19:46.760 --> 19:47.720
﻿Yeah!

19:47.720 --> 19:48.890
﻿Here's your money.

19:50.690 --> 19:51.430
﻿Boss...

19:52.480 --> 19:54.600
This is just a reward for one person, isn't it?

19:55.060 --> 19:59.190
﻿Of course it is! There's no way Lord Herman would try to cheat us!

19:59.190 --> 20:00.740
﻿You greedy scoundrels.

20:03.360 --> 20:05.030
﻿Thank you very much.

20:05.030 --> 20:09.450
﻿From now on, we shall be your loyal servants, m'lord.

20:10.580 --> 20:13.040
﻿Now my problem is what to do with this...

20:14.250 --> 20:15.420
﻿Who's there?!

20:18.550 --> 20:22.840
﻿I'm terribly sorry. The gate was open, so I walked in on my own.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.260
﻿You're...!

20:24.260 --> 20:25.300
﻿Do you know her?

20:26.100 --> 20:29.010
﻿She's a girl who was at the same orphanage as Nadja.

20:29.010 --> 20:32.980
﻿She said she knew a lot about Nadja, so we brought her here with us.

20:32.980 --> 20:35.480
﻿That brooch is Nadja's, isn't it?

20:35.650 --> 20:36.690
﻿W-We...

20:36.690 --> 20:38.480
﻿...were given that from Nadja!

20:38.480 --> 20:39.440
﻿You're lying.

20:39.900 --> 20:44.650
﻿Nadja always kept that precious to her, never parting with it.

20:44.990 --> 20:48.620
﻿There's no way she'd ever give it away to anyone.

20:49.330 --> 20:53.540
﻿I see... that's why you two were searching for her.

20:54.330 --> 20:56.330
﻿In order to steal that brooch from her.

20:57.080 --> 20:59.500
﻿It's something that has worth if it were stolen.

20:59.500 --> 21:02.800
﻿For example, it's very luxurious.

21:02.800 --> 21:06.010
﻿And it could act as proof to show that Nadja was the daughter of a noble.

21:06.930 --> 21:12.020
﻿was a maid at an aristocrat's mansion so I know very well of their world.

21:12.600 --> 21:15.980
﻿I don't think it would be too strange to find someone to do something like this.

21:16.560 --> 21:19.860
﻿It seems like you know a lot about Nadja.

21:19.860 --> 21:21.190
﻿What do you know?

21:21.400 --> 21:24.570
﻿Everything. I know that she's good at dancing.

21:24.570 --> 21:27.820
﻿I even know the same lullaby that she knows.

21:27.820 --> 21:30.660
﻿Do you know what kind of child Nadja is?

21:30.990 --> 21:32.040
﻿No...

21:32.040 --> 21:36.160
﻿She's blonde like myself and has the same blue eyes as me.

21:37.420 --> 21:40.340
﻿Is there anything I might be able to help you with?

21:44.630 --> 21:47.760
﻿Contact that bastard father of mine, I mean the Duke of Preminger...

21:47.760 --> 21:49.720
﻿Inform him that Nadja has been found.

21:51.720 --> 21:53.430
﻿What's your name?

21:53.430 --> 21:54.810
I go ﻿by Rosemary, m'lord.

21:54.810 --> 21:59.350
﻿Throw away that name. From today forward, your name is Nadja!

22:05.030 --> 22:05.610
﻿Yes.

